var e={id:`johannes-ved-jordan`,episode:17,door:17,title:{nb:`Johannes ved Jordan`,en:`John at the Jordan`},reference:`Luk 3,1–22`,place:`jeriko`,prologue:[{image:`maps/betlehem-dag.webp`,text:{nb:`Gutten fra fjellbygda, Sakarjas sønn, er blitt voksen. Nå står Johannes i Jordan, kledd i kamelhår, og hele landet går ned til ham.`,en:`The boy from the hill country, Zechariah’s son, has grown up. Now John stands in the Jordan, dressed in camel hair, and the whole land goes down to him.`}},{image:`art/lukas.webp`,text:{nb:`Lukas daterer det med sju navn. Og han lar noe pinlig stå: Jesus lot seg døpe av Johannes. Hvorfor tar han det med?`,en:`Luke dates it with seven names. And he lets something awkward stand: Jesus let himself be baptised by John. Why does he keep it in?`}}],intro:{nb:`Jeriko ved Jordan, tretti år etter, der noen ennå husker Johannes i elva.`,en:`Jericho by the Jordan, thirty years on, where some still remember John in the river.`},outro:{nb:`En datering med sju navn kan prøves. Det som er pinlig for ens egne, dikter man sjelden opp. Og Johannes sa selv nei til å være Messias.`,en:`A date with seven names can be checked. What embarrasses your own side is seldom made up. And John himself said he was not the Messiah.`},map:[`........########################`,`..#....#########################`,`###.....########################`,`###......#######################`,`######....######################`,`######.......###################`,`########.....###################`,`###########..###################`,`##########.........#..##########`,`#########.........###.##########`,`######............###.##########`,`###...............###....#######`,`####..#########.........########`,`####..#########.......##########`,`###############........#########`,`###############........#########`,`###############...##############`,`################..##############`,`################..##############`,`################..##############`,`###############...##############`],background:`jeriko-dag.webp`,mood:`calm`,areas:[{id:`vadestedet`,map:[`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`##.....#########################`,`##.....#########################`,`##.........#####################`,`#..##..#########################`,`...#############################`,`......##########################`,`............####################`,`##............##################`,`####..................##########`,`####..................##########`,`####...................#########`,`####.....................#######`,`#####......................#####`,`##...........................###`,`####..........................##`,`####..........................##`,`#####.........................##`,`#####........................###`],background:`jordan-elva.webp`,scale:1,ambience:`river`},{id:`skriverommet`,map:[`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`,`######.....#########......######`,`######......########......######`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#####......................#####`,`#############......#############`,`#############......#############`,`#############......#############`,`################################`,`################################`,`################################`],background:`skrivestue.webp`,scale:1.8,ambience:`street`}],start:{x:13,y:9},entities:[{id:`lukas`,kind:`person`,x:12,y:9,name:{nb:`Lukas`,en:`Luke`},look:`luke`,portrait:`lukas.webp`,interactions:[{not:[`oppdrag`],say:[{nb:`Snakk med disippelen, tolleren, soldaten, mannen fra ørkenen, skriveren og den gamle kona. Gå så ned til vadestedet og inn i skriverommet.`,en:`Talk to the disciple, the tax collector, the soldier, the man from the desert, the scribe and the old woman. Then go down to the ford and into the writing room.`}],set:[`oppdrag`]},{has:[`datering-lost`,`johannes-lost`,`daapen-lost`,`elia-lost`,`hva-gjore-lost`,`ved-elva-lost`],not:[`avsluttet`],say:[{nb:`Johannes sa selv at han ikke var Messias, men at en sterkere kom etter ham. Med den stemmen begynner jeg fortellingen om Jesus som voksen.`,en:`John said he was not the Messiah, but that someone stronger was coming. With that voice I begin the story of Jesus as a grown man.`},{nb:`I morgen: Galilea, og hva folk ventet seg.`,en:`Tomorrow: Galilee, and what people expected.`}],set:[`avsluttet`]},{has:[`spor:tidslinje`],not:[`datering-lost`],say:[{nb:`Sakene venter i vitneboka.`,en:`The cases are waiting in the notebook.`}]},{say:[{nb:`Disippelen, tolleren, soldaten, mannen fra ørkenen, skriveren fra Tiberias, den gamle kona. Vadestedet og skriverommet.`,en:`The disciple, the tax collector, the soldier, the man from the desert, the scribe from Tiberias, the old woman. The ford and the writing room.`}]}]},{id:`dor-skriverommet`,kind:`place`,x:22,y:11,name:{nb:`Skriverommet`,en:`The writing room`},look:`hotspot`,door:{area:`skriverommet`,x:15,y:14}},{id:`dor-vadestedet`,kind:`place`,x:16,y:19,name:{nb:`Ned til vadestedet`,en:`Down to the ford`},look:`hotspot`,door:{area:`vadestedet`,x:15,y:14},locked:{until:`sporene-lest`,say:{nb:`Hvilken sti går ned til vadestedet? Eseldriveren leser sporene i sanden.`,en:`Which path goes down to the ford? The donkey driver reads the tracks in the sand.`}}},{id:`disippel`,kind:`person`,x:9,y:6,name:{nb:`Johannes’ disippel`,en:`John’s disciple`},look:`james`,portrait:`james.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:disippel`],say:[{nb:`Jeg fulgte Johannes. Kamelhår, lærbelte, gresshopper og honning: ja, alt sammen. Han sto i elva og døpte dem som vendte om, og hele landet kom ned til ham.`,en:`I followed John. Camel hair, leather belt, locusts and honey: all of it. He stood in the river and baptised those who turned back to God, and the whole land came to him.`},{nb:`Folk spurte om han var Messias. Han sa nei, høyt: en sterkere kommer etter meg, og jeg er ikke god nok til å løse sandalene hans. Noen av oss holder sammen ennå, også i Efesos.`,en:`People asked if he was the Messiah. He said no, loudly: someone stronger is coming, and I am not fit to untie his sandals. Some of us still keep together, as far off as Ephesus.`},{nb:`Og ja: Jesus fra Nasaret kom også og lot seg døpe av ham. Jeg så det. Noen av oss skjønte ikke hvorfor den sterkere skulle døpes av den svakere.`,en:`And yes: Jesus of Nazareth came too and let himself be baptised by him. I saw it. Some of us did not understand why the stronger one should be baptised by the weaker.`}],set:[`spor:disippel`,`spor:ikke-messias`,`spor:daapen`,`fakta:johannes`]},{not:[`oppdrag`],say:[{nb:`Snakk med Lukas først.`,en:`Speak with Luke first.`}]},{say:[{nb:`Ikke Messias, sa han. En sterkere kommer.`,en:`Not the Messiah, he said. A stronger one is coming.`}]}]},{id:`toller`,kind:`person`,x:15,y:13,name:{nb:`Tolleren`,en:`The tax collector`},look:`trader`,portrait:`trader.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:toller`],say:[{nb:`Jeg gikk også ned til Johannes, med skammen min. «Hva skal vi gjøre?» spurte vi tollere. Han sa ikke: slutt. Han sa: ta ikke mer enn dere har rett til. Det kunne jeg gjøre.`,en:`I went down to John too, with my shame. “What should we do?” we tax collectors asked. He did not say stop. He said: take no more than you are owed. That I could do.`}],set:[`spor:toller`]},{say:[{nb:`Ikke mer enn jeg har rett til. Det holder jeg.`,en:`No more than I am entitled to. I stick to that.`}]}]},{id:`soldat`,kind:`person`,x:6,y:10,name:{nb:`Soldaten`,en:`The soldier`},look:`soldier`,portrait:`soldier.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:soldat`],say:[{nb:`Jeg tjente under Antipas da. Vi spurte også hva vi skulle gjøre. Han sa: ikke press penger av noen, ikke anklag falskt, vær fornøyd med lønna. Ikke: kast sverdet.`,en:`I served under Antipas then. We asked too. He said: don’t bully people for money or bring false charges, and live on your pay. He never said: throw away the sword.`},{nb:`Han var ingen opprører, enda kongen trodde det. Kongen lot ham fengsle i Makerus, borgen øst for Dødehavet, og der mistet han hodet.`,en:`He was no rebel, though the king thought so. The king locked him up at Machaerus, east of the Dead Sea, and there he was beheaded.`},{nb:`For Herodias’ skyld, sa folk; for roens skyld, sa kongen. Trolig begge deler.`,en:`For Herodias’ sake, people said; for the sake of order, said the king. Probably both.`}],set:[`spor:soldat`,`spor:makerus`,`fakta:makerus`]},{say:[{nb:`Makerus. Der endte det.`,en:`Machaerus. That is where it ended.`}]}]},{id:`essener`,kind:`person`,x:20,y:12,name:{nb:`Mannen fra ørkenen`,en:`The man from the desert`},look:`beggar`,portrait:`beggar.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:essener`],say:[{nb:`Vi ved Dødehavet renser oss i vann hver dag. Johannes døpte én gang, for den som vendte om, midt i elva, for alle, ikke bare for de hellige.`,en:`By the Dead Sea we wash every day. John baptised once, for anyone who turned back to God, out in the river, for everyone, not only the holy ones.`},{nb:`«Rydd vei i ørkenen», leser vi om oss selv. Johannes leste det om seg selv. Kanskje hadde han rett.`,en:`“Prepare the way in the wilderness”: we read that about ourselves. John read it about himself. Perhaps he was right.`}],set:[`spor:essener`,`fakta:daap`]},{say:[{nb:`Hver dag hos oss. Én gang hos ham.`,en:`Every day with us. Once with him.`}]}]},{id:`skriver`,kind:`person`,x:21,y:10,name:{nb:`Skriveren fra Tiberias`,en:`The scribe from Tiberias`},look:`scribe`,portrait:`scribe.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:skriver`],say:[{nb:`Jeg skrev ved hoffet til Antipas, kongen, som folk kalte ham. Johannes refset ham for ekteskapet med Herodias, brorens kone. Folkemengdene skremte ham mer enn ordene.`,en:`I wrote at Antipas’ court. John openly rebuked the king, as people called him, for marrying Herodias, his brother’s wife. And the crowds frightened the king more than the words.`},{nb:`Det året? Tiberius’ femtende år. Pilatus i Judea, Antipas i Galilea, broren Filip øst for sjøen, Lysanias i Abilene.`,en:`That year? Tiberius’ fifteenth year. Pilate in Judea, Antipas in Galilee, his brother Philip east of the lake, Lysanias in Abilene.`},{nb:`Og Annas og Kaifas som øversteprester, den ene etter den andre, og begge hadde makt. Spør hvem du vil.`,en:`And Annas and Caiaphas as high priests, one after the other, and both counted. Ask anyone.`},{nb:`Lysanias? Noen ler av det: Lysanias ble henrettet av Antonius lenge før Tiberius. Men det var den gamle.`,en:`Lysanias? Some laugh at that: Lysanias was executed by Antony long before Tiberius. But that was the old one.`},{nb:`Den unge Lysanias, tetrarken, er nevnt på en stein ved Abila fra Tiberius’ tid.`,en:`The young Lysanias, the tetrarch, has his name on a stone at Abila from the emperor’s own years.`}],set:[`spor:skriver`,`spor:herskerne`,`spor:lysanias`]},{say:[{nb:`Tiberius’ femtende år. Det året begynte det.`,en:`Tiberius’ fifteenth year. That year it began.`}]}]},{id:`kone`,kind:`person`,x:8,y:11,name:{nb:`Den gamle kona`,en:`The old woman`},look:`oldwoman`,portrait:`oldwoman.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:kone`],say:[{nb:`Alle gikk ned til elva den våren. Jeg også, ung kone. Vi sto i kø i det brune vannet. Han ropte om ormeyngel og om økser ved roten. Vi var redde og glade.`,en:`Everyone went down to the river that spring, me too, newly married. We stood in line in the brown water. He shouted about vipers and axes at the root. We were afraid and glad.`}],set:[`spor:kone`]},{say:[{nb:`Redde og glade. Slik var det ved elva.`,en:`Afraid and glad. That is how it was at the river.`}]}]},{id:`jente`,kind:`person`,x:12,y:5,name:{nb:`Jenta ved kilden`,en:`The girl at the spring`},look:`girl`,portrait:`girl.webp`,interactions:[{has:[],not:[`vannet-maalt`],say:[{nb:`Mor vil ha akkurat fem mål vann fra kilden til deigen, og jeg har bare krukka på tre og krukka på sju. Kan du måle det opp?`,en:`Mother wants exactly five measures of water from the spring for the dough, and I only have the three-measure jar and the seven. Can you measure it out?`}],play:{game:`jars`,title:{nb:`Mål opp vannet`,en:`Measure the water`},win:`vannet-maalt`,data:{a:3,b:7,goal:5,maxMoves:10}}},{say:[{nb:`Fem mål, akkurat. Mor blir fornøyd.`,en:`Five measures, exactly. Mother will be pleased.`}]}]},{id:`driver`,kind:`person`,x:17,y:16,name:{nb:`Eseldriveren`,en:`The donkey driver`},look:`driver`,portrait:`driver.webp`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Døperen ble ført til Makerus: over Jordan, sør langs Dødehavet, opp på fjellet, to dager herfra. Kongens borg, med utsikt over hele sjøen.`,en:`The Baptist was taken to Machaerus: across the Jordan, south along the Dead Sea and up the mountain, two days from here. The king’s fortress.`},{nb:`Alle slags folk gikk ned til elva for å høre ham. Les sporene i sanden, så finner du stien ned til vadestedet. Hvem gikk her?`,en:`All kinds of people went down to the river to hear him. Read the tracks in the sand to find the path to the ford. Who walked here?`}],set:[`spor:driver`],not:[`spor:driver`],play:{game:`tracks`,title:{nb:`Hvem gikk her?`,en:`Who walked here?`},win:`sporene-lest`,data:{rounds:6},key:!0}},{has:[`spor:driver`],say:[{nb:`Sporene i sanden igjen. Hvem gikk her?`,en:`The tracks in the sand again. Who walked here?`}],play:{game:`tracks`,title:{nb:`Hvem gikk her?`,en:`Who walked here?`},win:`sporene-lest`,data:{rounds:6},key:!0}}]},{id:`vei-jerusalem`,kind:`place`,x:0,y:0,name:{nb:`Opp til Jerusalem`,en:`Up to Jerusalem`},look:`hotspot`,travelTo:`jerusalem`},{id:`vei-nord`,kind:`place`,x:6,y:0,name:{nb:`Nordover til Galilea`,en:`North to Galilee`},look:`hotspot`,travelTo:`nasaret`},{id:`dor-ut-vadestedet`,kind:`place`,x:15,y:17,name:{nb:`Opp til byen`,en:`Up to the town`},look:`hotspot`,door:{area:`main`,x:16,y:18},area:`vadestedet`},{id:`elva`,kind:`thing`,x:12,y:10,name:{nb:`Jordan`,en:`The Jordan`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{has:[`vad:4`],not:[`vadet`],say:[{nb:`Brun, grunn og rask, med siv langs bredden. Vadestedet der veien fra Jeriko krysser over. Her, sier de, sto Johannes.`,en:`Brown, shallow and fast, with reeds along the bank. The ford where the road from Jericho crosses. Here, they say, John stood.`},{nb:`Grunt nok til å stå, dypt nok til å dukke. Du har kjent det selv.`,en:`Shallow enough to stand, deep enough to go under. You have felt it yourself.`}],set:[`vadet`,`spor:elva`]},{say:[{nb:`Brun, grunn og rask, med siv langs bredden. Vadestedet der veien fra Jeriko krysser over. Her, sier de, sto Johannes.`,en:`Brown, shallow and fast, with reeds along the bank. The ford where the road from Jericho crosses. Here, they say, John stood.`}],set:[`spor:elva`]}],area:`vadestedet`},{id:`kamelhaar`,kind:`thing`,x:24,y:14,name:{nb:`Kappa av kamelhår`,en:`The cloak of camel hair`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`En grov kappe av kamelhår og et lærbelte, hengt igjen av en disippel. Slik gikk profeten Elia kledd, sier Skriftene: en hårkappe og et lærbelte om livet.`,en:`A rough cloak of camel hair and a leather belt, left by a disciple. The Scriptures say the prophet Elijah dressed like that: a hairy cloak, a leather belt.`}],set:[`spor:kamelhaar`]}],area:`vadestedet`},{id:`pilegrim`,kind:`person`,x:18,y:11,name:{nb:`Pilegrimen ved elva`,en:`The pilgrim at the river`},look:`courier`,portrait:`courier.webp`,interactions:[{has:[`oppdrag`],not:[`spor:pilegrim`],say:[{nb:`Jeg kommer hit hvert år og går ut i vannet der han sto. Far ble døpt av ham. Far sa: han var ikke mild. Men han var ekte.`,en:`I come here every year and wade in where he stood. Father was baptised by him. Father said: he was not gentle. But he was real.`},{nb:`Han levde av gresshopper og vill honning, sa far. Det skulle jeg gjerne smakt én gang.`,en:`He lived on locusts and wild honey, Father said. I would like to taste that once.`}],set:[`spor:pilegrim`]},{has:[`honning`,`gresshopper`],not:[`maaltid-levert`],say:[{nb:`Ørkenmat, det han levde av. Ikke mild. Men ekte.`,en:`Desert food, what he lived on. Not mild. But real.`}],set:[`maaltid-levert`]},{say:[{nb:`Ikke mild. Men ekte.`,en:`Not gentle. But real.`}]}],area:`vadestedet`},{id:`dor-ut-skriverommet`,kind:`place`,x:15,y:17,name:{nb:`Ut på torget`,en:`Out to the square`},look:`hotspot`,door:{area:`main`,x:22,y:12},area:`skriverommet`},{id:`tidslinje`,kind:`thing`,x:8,y:7,name:{nb:`Lukas’ datering`,en:`Luke’s dating`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Slik har Lukas skrevet det: «I keiser Tiberius’ femtende år var Pontius Pilatus landshøvding i Judea. Herodes var fyrste over Galilea, broren Filip over Iturea og Trakonitis, og Lysanias over Abilene.»`,en:`As Luke has written it: “It was the fifteenth year of Emperor Tiberius. Pontius Pilate governed Judea, Herod Galilee, his brother Philip Ituraea and Trachonitis, and Lysanias Abilene.”`},{nb:`«Annas og Kaifas var øversteprester. Da kom Guds ord til Johannes, Sakarjas sønn, i ørkenen.» Sju navn, ett år.`,en:`“Annas and Caiaphas were high priests. And God’s word came to Zechariah’s son John out in the wilderness.” Seven names, one year.`}],set:[`spor:tidslinje`]}],area:`skriverommet`},{id:`jesaja`,kind:`thing`,x:22,y:7,name:{nb:`Rullen med Jesaja`,en:`The scroll of Isaiah`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Jesaja-rullen, åpnet der en røst roper i ørkenen: rydd Herrens vei og gjør stiene rette. Dalene fylles, fjellene senkes, og alle skal se Guds frelse. Johannes leste det om seg selv.`,en:`The Isaiah scroll, open at a voice calling in the wilderness: prepare the Lord’s way, make the paths straight, so all will see God’s salvation. John read it about himself.`}],set:[`spor:jesaja`]}],area:`skriverommet`},{id:`malaki`,kind:`thing`,x:26,y:9,name:{nb:`Rullen med de tolv profetene`,en:`The scroll of the twelve prophets`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Malaki: Gud sender sin budbærer foran seg for å rydde veien, og profeten Elia før Herrens dag. Elia gikk i hårkappe og lærbelte. Folk som så Johannes, tenkte på ham.`,en:`Malachi: God sends his messenger before him to prepare the way, and the prophet Elijah before the day of the Lord. Elijah wore a hairy cloak and a leather belt. People who saw John thought of him.`}],set:[`spor:malaki`]}],area:`skriverommet`},{id:`notat`,kind:`thing`,x:15,y:9,name:{nb:`Lukas’ notat`,en:`Luke’s note`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Et ark med strek under: «Alle vitnene sier det: Jesus ble døpt av Johannes, med en dåp til omvendelse. Noen disipler er forlegne over det. Jeg skriver det likevel, kort, for det skjedde.»`,en:`A sheet with a line under it: “All the witnesses say it: Jesus was baptised by John, with a baptism of repentance. Some disciples are embarrassed by it. I write it anyway, briefly, because it happened.”`},{nb:`«Og det som skjedde etterpå: himmelen åpen, Ånden, en røst.»`,en:`“And what happened afterwards: heaven open, the Spirit, a voice.”`}],set:[`spor:notat`]}],area:`skriverommet`},{id:`stein-1`,kind:`thing`,x:9,y:9,name:{nb:`En vadestein`,en:`A ford stone`},look:`hotspot`,area:`vadestedet`,interactions:[{has:[`spor:kone`],not:[`vad:1`],say:[{nb:`Første stein. Brunt vann til knes, slik kona sa.`,en:`First stone. Brown water to the knees, as the woman said.`}],set:[`vad:1`]},{has:[`vad:1`],say:[{nb:`Du har stått her.`,en:`You have stood here.`}]},{say:[{nb:`Hør den gamle kona om køen ved elva først.`,en:`Hear the old woman about the queue at the river first.`}]}]},{id:`stein-2`,kind:`thing`,x:5,y:8,name:{nb:`En vadestein`,en:`A ford stone`},look:`hotspot`,area:`vadestedet`,interactions:[{has:[`vad:1`],not:[`vad:2`],say:[{nb:`Andre stein. Her sto køen og ventet.`,en:`Second stone. Here the line stood waiting.`}],set:[`vad:2`]},{has:[`vad:2`],say:[{nb:`Du har stått her.`,en:`You have stood here.`}]},{say:[{nb:`Gå steinene i rekkefølge, fra bredden.`,en:`Take the stones in order, from the bank.`}]}]},{id:`stein-3`,kind:`thing`,x:6,y:6,name:{nb:`En vadestein`,en:`A ford stone`},look:`hotspot`,area:`vadestedet`,interactions:[{has:[`vad:2`],not:[`vad:3`],say:[{nb:`Tredje stein. Strømmen drar i beina.`,en:`Third stone. The current pulls at your legs.`}],set:[`vad:3`]},{has:[`vad:3`],say:[{nb:`Du har stått her.`,en:`You have stood here.`}]},{say:[{nb:`Gå steinene i rekkefølge, fra bredden.`,en:`Take the stones in order, from the bank.`}]}]},{id:`stein-4`,kind:`thing`,x:10,y:5,name:{nb:`En vadestein`,en:`A ford stone`},look:`hotspot`,area:`vadestedet`,interactions:[{has:[`vad:3`],not:[`vad:4`],say:[{nb:`Midt i elva. Her sto han.`,en:`In the middle of the river. Here he stood.`}],set:[`vad:4`]},{has:[`vad:4`],say:[{nb:`Du har stått her.`,en:`You have stood here.`}]},{say:[{nb:`Gå steinene i rekkefølge, fra bredden.`,en:`Take the stones in order, from the bank.`}]}]},{id:`bikube`,kind:`thing`,x:4,y:4,name:{nb:`Bikuben`,en:`The beehive`},look:`hotspot`,area:`vadestedet`,interactions:[{has:[`spor:disippel`],not:[`honning`],say:[{nb:`Vill honning fra en sprekk i fjellet. Du tar litt med.`,en:`Wild honey from a crack in the rock. You take some with you.`}],set:[`honning`]},{say:[{nb:`En sprekk i fjellet der biene går inn og ut.`,en:`A crack in the rock where bees come and go.`}]}]},{id:`sivet`,kind:`thing`,x:26,y:16,name:{nb:`Sivet`,en:`The reeds`},look:`hotspot`,area:`vadestedet`,interactions:[{has:[`spor:disippel`],not:[`gresshopper`],say:[{nb:`Gresshopper i sivet. Rene å spise, sier loven.`,en:`Locusts in the reeds. Clean to eat, says the law.`}],set:[`gresshopper`]},{say:[{nb:`Siv langs bredden. Det surrer der inne.`,en:`Reeds along the bank. Something is buzzing in there.`}]}]},{id:`leke-frukt`,kind:`thing`,x:15,y:8,name:{nb:`Fruktboden`,en:`The fruit stall`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Fikenene triller. Tolleren plukker opp en: «Den regner jeg som avgift.» Selgeren er ikke enig.`,en:`The figs roll away. The tax collector picks one up: “I’ll count that as duty.” The seller does not agree.`}],fx:`tip`}]},{id:`leke-tonne`,kind:`thing`,x:4,y:11,name:{nb:`Tønna`,en:`The barrel`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Du banker tre ganger. En soldat roper: «Hvem er det som banker?» Det er bare deg.`,en:`Three knocks. A soldier shouts: “Who is knocking?” It is only you.`}],fx:`knock`}]},{id:`leke-bru`,kind:`thing`,x:5,y:13,name:{nb:`Brua over kanalen`,en:`The bridge over the canal`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Plask! Det er ikke Jordan, men vannet er like kaldt.`,en:`Splash! It isn’t the Jordan, but the water is just as cold.`}],fx:`splash`}]},{id:`leke-busk`,kind:`thing`,x:17,y:10,name:{nb:`Busken`,en:`The bush`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Busken rister, og gresshopper spretter til alle kanter. Mannen fra ørkenen ser interessert ut.`,en:`The bush shakes and locusts spring out in every direction. The man from the desert looks interested.`}],fx:`shake`}]},{id:`leke-duer`,kind:`thing`,x:19,y:14,name:{nb:`Duene`,en:`The doves`},look:`hotspot`,interactions:[{say:[{nb:`Duene letter og flyr østover, mot elva.`,en:`The doves fly up and head east, towards the river.`}],fx:`scatter`}]}],facts:[{id:`johannes`,title:{nb:`Johannes hos Josefus`,en:`John in Josephus`},body:{nb:`Den jødiske historikeren Josefus (Antiquitates 18,116–119, skrevet ca. år 93) forteller uavhengig av evangeliene at Johannes var en god mann som ba jødene leve rett og la seg døpe, at folkemengdene fulgte ham, og at Herodes Antipas fryktet opprør og lot ham henrette i borgen Makerus. Evangeliene gir Herodias som grunn, Josefus politikken; de to passer godt sammen. Dette er en av de beste ytre bekreftelsene av en person i evangeliene.`,en:`The Jewish historian Josephus (Antiquities 18.116–119, written c. AD 93) tells independently of the Gospels that John was a good man who told the Jews to live rightly and be baptised, that the crowds followed him, and that Herod Antipas feared revolt and had him executed at the fortress of Machaerus. The Gospels give Herodias as the reason, Josephus the politics; the two fit well together. This is one of the best external confirmations of a person in the Gospels.`},unlockedBy:`fakta:johannes`,link:`https://bibleproject.com/videos/character-insight-john-baptizer/`},{id:`synkronisme`,title:{nb:`Sju navn for ett år`,en:`Seven names for one year`},body:{nb:`Luk 3,1–2 daterer Johannes’ opptreden med sju navn i seks ledd (Annas og Kaifas deler øversteprestleddet): Tiberius’ femtende år (28/29), Pilatus (prefekt 26–36), Herodes Antipas (4 f.Kr.–39), Filip (4 f.Kr.–34), Lysanias av Abilene (lenge regnet som Lukas’ feil, fordi Josefus’ Lysanias ble henrettet på Marcus Antonius’ ordre i 36 f.Kr., i Herodes den stores første år som konge; en innskrift fra Abila fra Tiberius’ tid nevner en yngre tetrark Lysanias, som passer), og Annas og Kaifas (Annas avsatt i år 15, men fortsatt mektig; Kaifas 18–36). Det er den grundigste dateringen i hele Det nye testamente, og ingen av leddene er motbevist. At «begge hadde makt»: Annas var avsatt, men regnet fortsatt som øversteprest av mange (jf. Joh 18,13; Apg 4,6). Antipas var tetrark, ikke konge, men Markus kaller ham kong Herodes (Mark 6,14), slik folk nok gjorde.`,en:`Luke 3:1–2 dates John’s appearance with seven names in six items (Annas and Caiaphas share the high-priestly item): Tiberius’ fifteenth year (AD 28/29), Pilate (prefect 26–36), Herod Antipas (4 BC–AD 39), Philip (4 BC–AD 34), Lysanias of Abilene (long counted as Luke’s error, since Josephus’ Lysanias was executed on Mark Antony’s orders in 36 BC, early in Herod the Great’s reign; an inscription from Abila from Tiberius’ time names a younger tetrarch Lysanias, which fits), and Annas and Caiaphas (Annas deposed in AD 15 but still powerful; Caiaphas 18–36). It is the most thorough dating in the whole New Testament, and none of the items has been disproved. Annas and Caiaphas both “counted”: Annas had been deposed, but many still treated him as high priest (cf. John 18:13; Acts 4:6). Antipas was a tetrarch, not a king, but Mark calls him King Herod (Mark 6:14), as people probably did.`},unlockedBy:`datering-lost`},{id:`daap`,title:{nb:`Dåp og renselse`,en:`Baptism and washing`},body:{nb:`Kort sagt: At Jesus lot seg døpe, var pinlig for de første kristne, og derfor tror nesten alle at det skjedde. Jødene kjente rituell renselse i vann (mikve), og samfunnet ved Qumran renset seg daglig. Johannes’ dåp var annerledes: én gang, for den som vendte om, og for alle. Senere jødiske kilder forteller at hedninger som ble jøder, også ble neddykket; om skikken fantes alt på Johannes’ tid, er omdiskutert. At Jesus lot seg døpe med «en dåp til omvendelse» (Luk 3,3), var forlegent for de første kristne (Matteus lar Johannes protestere, Matt 3,14), og regnes derfor av nesten alle forskere som historisk. Legg merke til hvordan Lukas selv forteller det: han nevner fengslingen av Johannes (3,19–20) før dåpen (3,21), og skriver bare at Jesus ble døpt, uten å si av hvem. Markus sier det rett ut, Matteus lar Johannes protestere, Lukas sier det kort, Johannesevangeliet nevner ikke selve dåpen. Jo mer forlegne, desto kortere, og likevel står det. Det pinlige var dobbelt: en dåp til tilgivelse for synder for en de mente var uten synd, og den mindre som døper den større. Samfunnet ved Qumran leste også Jesaja-ordet om røsten i ørkenen om seg selv (1QS 8,13–14; Jes 40,3).`,en:`In short, that Jesus was baptised embarrassed the first Christians, which is why nearly all think it happened. The Jews knew ritual washing in water (mikveh), and the community at Qumran washed daily. John’s baptism was different: once, for the one who turned back to God, and for everyone. Later Jewish sources say that gentiles becoming Jews were also immersed; whether the custom already existed in John’s day is debated. That Jesus let himself be baptised with “a baptism of repentance” (Luke 3:3) was embarrassing for the first Christians (Matthew has John protest, Matt 3:14), and is therefore counted historical by nearly all scholars. Notice how Luke himself tells it: he mentions John’s imprisonment (3:19–20) before the baptism (3:21), and writes only that Jesus was baptised, without saying by whom. Mark says it plainly, Matthew has John protest, Luke says it briefly, John’s Gospel does not mention the baptism itself. The more embarrassed, the shorter, and still it stands. The awkwardness was double: a baptism for the forgiveness of sins for one they held to be without sin, and the lesser baptising the greater. The Qumran community also read Isaiah’s words about the voice in the wilderness as being about themselves (1QS 8:13–14; Isa 40:3).`},unlockedBy:`fakta:daap`},{id:`makerus`,title:{nb:`Makerus`,en:`Machaerus`},body:{nb:`Makerus var en fjellborg øst for Dødehavet, bygd av hasmoneerne og utvidet av Herodes den store. Josefus sier at Johannes ble henrettet der. Borgen er gravd ut; palasset, badet og sisternene er funnet. Herodes Antipas giftet seg med Herodias, sin halvbrors kone, og den avviste første kona var datter av nabateerkongen Aretas, som senere slo Antipas i krig; Josefus sier folk så nederlaget som straff for Johannes. To kjente spørsmål: Markus kaller Herodias’ første mann Filip, Josefus kaller ham Herodes; og Josefus nevner Johannes i et tilbakeblikk fra Aretas’ seier i år 36, som ikke daterer henrettelsen.`,en:`Machaerus was a mountain fortress east of the Dead Sea, built by the Hasmoneans and enlarged by Herod the Great. Josephus says John was executed there. The fortress has been excavated; the palace, the bath and the cisterns have been found. Herod Antipas married Herodias, his half-brother’s wife, and the rejected first wife was the daughter of the Nabataean king Aretas, who later defeated Antipas in war; Josephus says people saw the defeat as punishment for John. Two well-known problems: Mark calls Herodias’ first husband Philip, Josephus calls him Herod; and Josephus mentions John in a flashback from Aretas’ victory in AD 36, which does not date the execution.`},unlockedBy:`fakta:makerus`},{id:`elia`,title:{nb:`Johannes og Elia`,en:`John and Elijah`},body:{nb:`Elia gikk i hårkappe og lærbelte (2 Kong 1,8), og Malaki lovte at Elia skulle komme før Herrens dag (Mal 3,23; 4,5 i engelske bibler). Johannes kledde seg slik (Mark 1,6), men svarte nei da han ble spurt om han var Elia (Joh 1,21). Engelen hadde sagt at han skulle gå fram «i Elias ånd og kraft» (Luk 1,17), og Jesus sa at Elia «er kommet» (Mark 9,13). Evangeliene lar spenningen stå.`,en:`Elijah wore a hairy cloak and a leather belt (2 Kgs 1:8), and Malachi promised Elijah would come before the day of the Lord (Mal 4:5). John dressed that way (Mark 1:6), but answered no when asked whether he was Elijah (John 1:21). The angel had said he would go “in the spirit and power of Elijah” (Luke 1:17), and Jesus said Elijah “has come” (Mark 9:13). The Gospels let the tension stand.`},unlockedBy:`elia-lost`},{id:`disiplene`,title:{nb:`Johannes’ disipler`,en:`John’s disciples`},body:{nb:`Johannes hadde egne disipler som fastet og ba (Luk 5,33), og som fortsatte etter hans død; Paulus møtte en flokk av dem i Efesos omkring år 52 (Apg 19,1–7). At bevegelsen levde videre ved siden av de kristne, taler mot at kristne har diktet Johannes til et vitne om Jesus: de måtte forholde seg til ham som han var. Samtidig er det tydelig at evangeliene former Johannes i retning av Jesus, sterkest i Joh 1,6–8 og 1,20. Det kritikere spør om, er hvor mye. Det Josefus sikrer, er kjernen: en selvstendig profet med egen dåp og egne disipler, henrettet av Antipas.`,en:`John had his own disciples who fasted and prayed (Luke 5:33), and who carried on after his death; Paul met a group of them in Ephesus around AD 52 (Acts 19:1–7). That the movement lived on beside the Christians tells against Christians having invented John as a witness to Jesus: they had to deal with him as he was. At the same time the Gospels clearly shape John towards Jesus, most strongly in John 1:6–8 and 1:20. What critics ask is how much. What Josephus secures is the core: an independent prophet with his own baptism and his own disciples, executed by Antipas.`},unlockedBy:`johannes-lost`},{id:`diktet`,title:{nb:`Hva er funnet på i denne episoden?`,en:`What is made up in this episode?`},unlockedBy:`ved-elva-lost`,body:{nb:`Disippelen, tolleren, soldaten, mannen fra ørkenen, skriveren fra Tiberias, den gamle kona, jenta, eseldriveren og pilegrimen er funnet på, og det samme er det de sier. Kappa ved elva, vadesteinene, skriverommet og Lukas’ ark er laget for spillet. Hvor ved Jordan Johannes døpte, vet vi ikke sikkert. Johannes selv er godt kjent, fra Luk 3,1–22 og fra Josefus, som forteller om dåpen og om henrettelsen i Makerus.`,en:`The disciple, the tax collector, the soldier, the man from the desert, the scribe from Tiberias, the old woman, the girl, the donkey driver and the pilgrim are invented, and so is what they say. The cloak by the river, the stepping stones, the writing room and Luke’s sheets are made for the game. Where on the Jordan John baptised, we do not know for sure. John himself is well known, from Luke 3:1–22 and from Josephus, who tells of his baptism and of his execution at Machaerus.`}}],clues:[{id:`tidslinje`,source:{nb:`Lukas’ datering`,en:`Luke’s dating`},text:{nb:`Tiberius’ femtende år, Pilatus, Herodes, Filip, Lysanias, Annas og Kaifas: sju navn for ett år.`,en:`Tiberius’ fifteenth year, Pilate, Herod, Philip, Lysanias, Annas and Caiaphas: seven names for one year.`},unlockedBy:`spor:tidslinje`},{id:`herskerne`,source:{nb:`Skriveren fra Tiberias`,en:`The scribe from Tiberias`},text:{nb:`Han husker det samme året: Tiberius i sitt femtende år, Pilatus i Judea, Antipas i Galilea, Filip øst for sjøen, Lysanias i Abilene, Annas og Kaifas.`,en:`He remembers the same year: Tiberius in his fifteenth year, Pilate in Judea, Antipas in Galilee, Philip east of the lake, Lysanias in Abilene, Annas and Caiaphas.`},unlockedBy:`spor:herskerne`},{id:`lysanias`,source:{nb:`Skriveren fra Tiberias`,en:`The scribe from Tiberias`},text:{nb:`To menn het Lysanias: den gamle, henrettet av Antonius lenge før Tiberius, og den unge tetrarken i Abilene, navngitt på en stein fra Tiberius’ år.`,en:`Two men were called Lysanias: the old one, executed by Antony long before Tiberius, and the young tetrarch in Abilene, named on a stone from Tiberius’ years.`},unlockedBy:`spor:lysanias`},{id:`disippel`,source:{nb:`Johannes’ disippel`,en:`John’s disciple`},text:{nb:`Kamelhår, lærbelte, gresshopper og honning. Han sto i elva og døpte dem som vendte om; hele landet kom ned.`,en:`Camel hair, leather belt, locusts and honey. He stood in the river and baptised those who turned back to God; the whole land came down.`},unlockedBy:`spor:disippel`},{id:`ikke-messias`,source:{nb:`Johannes’ disippel`,en:`John’s disciple`},text:{nb:`Johannes sa høyt at han ikke var Messias: en sterkere kommer etter meg. Noen holder sammen etter ham ennå, helt til Efesos.`,en:`John said loudly that he was not the Messiah: a stronger one comes after me. Some still stick together, even now he is gone, as far away as Ephesus.`},unlockedBy:`spor:ikke-messias`},{id:`daapen`,source:{nb:`Johannes’ disippel`,en:`John’s disciple`},text:{nb:`Jesus kom og lot seg døpe av Johannes. Noen av oss skjønte ikke hvorfor den sterkere skulle døpes av den svakere.`,en:`Jesus came and let himself be baptised by John. Some of us did not understand why the stronger should be baptised by the weaker.`},unlockedBy:`spor:daapen`},{id:`notat`,source:{nb:`Lukas’ notat`,en:`Luke’s note`},text:{nb:`Alle vitnene sier at Jesus ble døpt av Johannes, med en dåp til omvendelse. Noen er forlegne. Lukas skriver det likevel.`,en:`All the witnesses say Jesus was baptised by John, with a baptism of repentance. Some are embarrassed. Luke writes it anyway.`},unlockedBy:`spor:notat`},{id:`toller`,source:{nb:`Tolleren`,en:`The tax collector`},text:{nb:`Johannes sa ikke «slutt å være toller», men «ta ikke mer enn dere har rett til».`,en:`John did not say “stop being a tax collector”, but “take no more than you are entitled to”.`},unlockedBy:`spor:toller`},{id:`soldat`,source:{nb:`Soldaten`,en:`The soldier`},text:{nb:`Til soldatene: ikke press penger av noen, ikke anklag falskt, vær fornøyd med lønna. Ikke en opprører, enda kongen trodde det.`,en:`To the soldiers: do not extort, do not accuse falsely, be content with your pay. Not a rebel, though the king thought so.`},unlockedBy:`spor:soldat`},{id:`makerus`,source:{nb:`Soldaten`,en:`The soldier`},text:{nb:`Antipas fengslet Johannes i Makerus og lot ham henrette. For Herodias’ skyld, sa folk; for roens skyld, sa kongen.`,en:`Antipas imprisoned John at Machaerus and had him executed. For Herodias’ sake, people said; for the sake of order, the king said.`},unlockedBy:`spor:makerus`},{id:`skriver`,source:{nb:`Skriveren fra Tiberias`,en:`The scribe from Tiberias`},text:{nb:`Johannes refset kongen åpent for ekteskapet med Herodias. Folkemengdene skremte kongen mer enn ordene.`,en:`John rebuked the king openly for the marriage to Herodias. The crowds frightened the king more than the words.`},unlockedBy:`spor:skriver`},{id:`essener`,source:{nb:`Mannen fra ørkenen`,en:`The man from the desert`},text:{nb:`Ved Dødehavet renser de seg hver dag; Johannes døpte én gang, i elva, for alle som vendte om.`,en:`By the Dead Sea they wash every day; John baptised once, in the river, for all who turned back to God.`},unlockedBy:`spor:essener`},{id:`kamelhaar`,source:{nb:`Det du selv så`,en:`What you saw yourself`},text:{nb:`Kappe av kamelhår og lærbelte: slik gikk Elia kledd.`,en:`A cloak of camel hair and a leather belt: that is how Elijah dressed.`},unlockedBy:`spor:kamelhaar`},{id:`malaki`,source:{nb:`Rullen med de tolv profetene`,en:`The scroll of the twelve prophets`},text:{nb:`Budbæreren som rydder veien, og Elia før Herrens dag.`,en:`The messenger who prepares the way, and Elijah before the day of the Lord.`},unlockedBy:`spor:malaki`},{id:`jesaja`,source:{nb:`Rullen med Jesaja`,en:`The scroll of Isaiah`},text:{nb:`En røst roper i ørkenen: rydd Herrens vei. Johannes leste det om seg selv.`,en:`A voice cries in the wilderness: prepare the way of the Lord. John read it about himself.`},unlockedBy:`spor:jesaja`},{id:`kone`,source:{nb:`Den gamle kona`,en:`The old woman`},text:{nb:`Alle gikk ned til elva den våren og sto i kø i vannet. Han ropte om ormeyngel og økser. Redde og glade.`,en:`Everyone went down to the river that spring and stood in line in the water. He shouted about vipers and axes. Afraid and glad.`},unlockedBy:`spor:kone`},{id:`elva`,source:{nb:`Det du selv så`,en:`What you saw yourself`},text:{nb:`Vadestedet der veien fra Jeriko krysser Jordan. Her sto han, sier de.`,en:`The ford where the road from Jericho crosses the Jordan. Here he stood, they say.`},unlockedBy:`spor:elva`}],deductions:[{id:`datering`,question:{nb:`Noen sier Lysanias er en feil i lista mi. Er det det?`,en:`Some say Lysanias is a mistake in my list. Is it?`},clues:[`tidslinje`,`herskerne`,`lysanias`],steps:[{ask:{nb:`Hva står på dateringsarket mitt i skriverommet?`,en:`What is on my dating sheet in the scribes’ room?`},clues:[`tidslinje`],yes:{nb:`Sju navn, og Lysanias i Abilene blant dem. Hva sa skriveren?`,en:`Seven names, and Lysanias in Abilene among them. What did the scribe say?`},no:{nb:`Det er ikke dateringsarket.`,en:`That is not the dating sheet.`}},{ask:{nb:`Hva sa skriveren fra Tiberias om det året, og om Lysanias?`,en:`What did the scribe from Tiberias say about that year, and about Lysanias?`},clues:[`herskerne`,`lysanias`],yes:{nb:`De samme navnene, og to menn som het Lysanias. Er navnet en feil?`,en:`The same names, and two men called Lysanias. Is the name a mistake?`},no:{nb:`Ikke den lappen. Jeg spør hva skriveren husket om det året og om Lysanias.`,en:`Not that note. I am asking what the scribe remembered about that year and about Lysanias.`}}],options:[{text:{nb:`Nei. Det fantes en yngre Lysanias i Abilene på Tiberius’ tid`,en:`No. There was a younger Lysanias in Abilene under Tiberius`},feedback:{nb:`Riktig. Noe blir ofte kalt feil fordi en brikke mangler, og så dukker brikken opp. Jeg har ikke alltid rett, men «ingen andre nevner det» er ikke det samme som «det er galt».`,en:`Correct. Things are often called mistakes because a piece is missing, and then the piece turns up. I am not always right, but “nobody else mentions it” does not mean “it is wrong”.`},correct:!0},{text:{nb:`Ja. Lukas har blandet inn den gamle Lysanias`,en:`Yes. Luke has mixed the old Lysanias into Tiberius’ time`},feedback:{nb:`Nei. Les skriverens ord en gang til: det var to med samme navn.`,en:`No. Read the scribe’s words once more: there were two with the same name.`}},{text:{nb:`Det spiller ingen rolle; ett navn endrer ingenting`,en:`It makes no difference; one name changes nothing`},feedback:{nb:`Jo. Hvert navn er en dør for den som vil prøve meg. Hadde jeg bommet her, ville Teofilos spurt hva annet jeg bommet på.`,en:`It does. Every name is a door for anyone who wants to test me. Had I slipped here, Theophilus would have asked what else I slipped on.`}}],set:[`datering-lost`]},{id:`johannes`,question:{nb:`Hvem var Johannes, og hva sa han om seg selv?`,en:`Who was John, and what did he say about himself?`},clues:[`disippel`,`ikke-messias`,`skriver`],steps:[{ask:{nb:`Hva sa disippelen om hvordan Johannes så ut, og om han var Messias?`,en:`What did the disciple say about how John looked, and about whether he was the Messiah?`},clues:[`disippel`,`ikke-messias`],yes:{nb:`Kamelhår, dåp i elva, og «jeg er ikke Messias». Hva sa skriveren om ham og kongen?`,en:`Camel hair, baptism in the river, and “I am not the Messiah”. What did the scribe say about him and the king?`},no:{nb:`Ikke den lappen; det handler ikke om Johannes selv.`,en:`Not that note; it is not about John himself.`}},{ask:{nb:`Hva sa skriveren fra Tiberias om Johannes og kongen?`,en:`What did the scribe from Tiberias say about John and the king?`},clues:[`skriver`],yes:{nb:`Han refset kongen åpent, og kongen fryktet mengden. Hvem var han?`,en:`He rebuked the king openly, and the king feared the crowds. Who was he?`},no:{nb:`Det er ikke skriveren om Johannes og kongen.`,en:`That is not the scribe on John and the king.`}}],options:[{text:{nb:`En profet som døpte dem som vendte om, og som selv sa at han ikke var Messias`,en:`A prophet who baptised those who turned back, and said he was not the Messiah`},feedback:{nb:`Riktig. Han sa at en sterkere kom etter ham. Hans disipler holder sammen ennå; hadde jeg diktet noe om Johannes, ville de sagt fra.`,en:`Right. He said a stronger one was coming after him. His disciples still keep together; had I made anything up about John, they would have spoken up.`},correct:!0},{text:{nb:`En opprører som samlet folk ved elva for å styrte kongen og drive ut romerne`,en:`A rebel who gathered people at the river to overthrow the king and drive out the Romans`},feedback:{nb:`Nei. Han ba soldatene være fornøyd med lønna og tollerne ta rett sum. Kongen fryktet mengden, ikke sverd.`,en:`No. He told the soldiers to be content with their pay and the tax collectors to take the right sum. The king feared the crowd, not swords.`}},{text:{nb:`Messias selv, som disiplene hans fortsatt tror, helt til Efesos`,en:`The Messiah himself, as his disciples still believe, as far away as Ephesus`},feedback:{nb:`Nei. Han sa nei, høyt, og disippelen hørte det. At flokken hans holder sammen, betyr ikke at de kaller ham Messias.`,en:`No. He said no, loudly, and the disciple heard it. That his group keeps together does not mean they call him the Messiah.`}}],set:[`johannes-lost`]},{id:`daapen`,question:{nb:`Hvorfor tar Lukas med at Jesus ble døpt, når det var pinlig?`,en:`Why does Luke include that Jesus was baptised, when it was awkward?`},clues:[`daapen`,`notat`],steps:[{ask:{nb:`Hva sa disippelen om Jesus ved elva?`,en:`What did the disciple say about Jesus at the river?`},clues:[`daapen`],yes:{nb:`Han lot seg døpe, og noen skjønte det ikke. Hva står i notatet mitt?`,en:`He let himself be baptised, and some did not understand. What is in my note?`},no:{nb:`Det er ikke det disippelen sa om Jesus.`,en:`That is not what the disciple said about Jesus.`}},{ask:{nb:`Hva står i notatet mitt om dåpen?`,en:`What is in my note on the baptism?`},clues:[`notat`],yes:{nb:`Alle vitnene sier det, noen er forlegne, jeg skriver det likevel. Hvorfor?`,en:`All the witnesses say it, some are embarrassed, I write it anyway. Why?`},no:{nb:`Det er ikke notatet mitt.`,en:`That is not my note.`}}],options:[{text:{nb:`Fordi det skjedde, og alle vitnene sier det; noe så pinlig dikter man sjelden opp`,en:`Because it happened, and all the witnesses say so; such awkward things are seldom made up`},feedback:{nb:`Riktig. En dåp til omvendelse var pinlig for oss, derfor skriver jeg det kort. Men jeg skriver det.`,en:`Right. A baptism of repentance was awkward for us, so I write it briefly. But I write it.`},correct:!0},{text:{nb:`Fordi Johannes var viktigere enn Jesus, og Lukas ville vise hvem som var den største`,en:`Because John was more important than Jesus, and Luke wanted to show who was the greater`},feedback:{nb:`Nei. Johannes sa selv det motsatte: en sterkere kommer. Nettopp derfor er dåpen pinlig, og nettopp derfor står den.`,en:`No. John himself said the opposite: a stronger one is coming. That is exactly why the baptism is awkward, and exactly why it stands.`}},{text:{nb:`Det står ikke at Jesus ble døpt; Lukas skriver bare at han sto ved elva og ba`,en:`It does not say Jesus was baptised; Luke writes only that he stood by the river and prayed`},feedback:{nb:`Jo. Disippelen så det, alle vitnene sier det, og jeg skriver at han ble døpt. Kort, men det står.`,en:`It does. The disciple saw it, all the witnesses say it, and I write that he was baptised. Briefly, but it stands.`}}],set:[`daapen-lost`]},{id:`elia`,question:{nb:`Hvorfor tenkte folk på Elia når de så Johannes, og hadde de rett?`,en:`Why did people think of Elijah when they saw John, and were they right?`},clues:[`kamelhaar`,`malaki`,`jesaja`],steps:[{ask:{nb:`Hvilken kappe så du ved elva, og hva står hos Malaki?`,en:`Which cloak did you see by the river, and what is in Malachi?`},clues:[`kamelhaar`,`malaki`],yes:{nb:`Hårkappe og lærbelte, som Elia, og Elia før Herrens dag. Hva leste Johannes selv om seg?`,en:`Dressed like Elijah, and Elijah comes before the day of the Lord. What did John read about himself?`},no:{nb:`Det handler ikke om Elia.`,en:`That is not about Elijah.`}},{ask:{nb:`Hva står i rullen med Jesaja?`,en:`What is in the scroll of Isaiah?`},clues:[`jesaja`],yes:{nb:`En røst i ørkenen som rydder veien. Hadde folk rett om Elia?`,en:`A voice in the wilderness preparing the way. Were people right about Elijah?`},no:{nb:`Det er ikke Jesaja.`,en:`That is not Isaiah.`}}],options:[{text:{nb:`Kappa og ordene om å rydde veien pekte på Elia. Selv kalte Johannes seg bare en røst i ørkenen`,en:`The cloak and the words about preparing the way pointed to Elijah. John himself claimed only to be a voice in the wilderness`},feedback:{nb:`Riktig. Engelen sa at han skulle gå fram i Elias ånd og kraft, og selv tok han bare Jesajas ord: en røst. Begge deler står, og det er ærlig å la dem stå.`,en:`Correct. The angel said he would go in the spirit and power of Elijah, and he himself took only Isaiah’s words: a voice. Both stand, and it is honest to let them stand.`},correct:!0},{text:{nb:`Johannes var Elia selv, kommet tilbake fra himmelen i den samme kappa`,en:`John was Elijah himself, come back down from heaven wearing the very same cloak`},feedback:{nb:`Nei. Han var Sakarjas sønn, født i fjellbygda, og vi kjenner mor og far. «I Elias ånd og kraft», sa engelen, ikke Elia selv.`,en:`No. He was Zechariah’s son, born in the hill country, and we know his mother and father. “In the spirit and power of Elijah”, the angel said, not Elijah himself.`}},{text:{nb:`Ingen tenkte på Elia; kamelhår var bare det alle i ørkenen gikk med`,en:`Nobody thought of Elijah; camel hair was simply what everyone in the desert wore`},feedback:{nb:`Jo. Se kappa og lærbeltet: slik beskrives Elia. Mange som kjente Skriftene, tenkte det, og de spurte ham.`,en:`They did. Look at the cloak and the leather belt: that is how Elijah is described. Many who knew the Scriptures thought it, and they asked him.`}}],set:[`elia-lost`]},{id:`hva-gjore`,question:{nb:`Hva sa Johannes til tollere og soldater, og hva sier det om ham?`,en:`What did John say to tax collectors and soldiers, and what does it say about him?`},clues:[`toller`,`soldat`,`essener`],steps:[{ask:{nb:`Hva sa tolleren og soldaten at Johannes svarte dem?`,en:`What did the tax collector and the soldier say John answered them?`},clues:[`toller`,`soldat`],yes:{nb:`Ta ikke mer enn dere har rett til; vær fornøyd med lønna. Hva sa mannen fra ørkenen?`,en:`Take no more than you are owed; live on your pay. What did the man from the desert say?`},no:{nb:`Ikke den lappen. Jeg spør hva Johannes svarte tolleren og soldaten.`,en:`Not that note. I am asking what John answered the tax collector and the soldier.`}},{ask:{nb:`Hva sa mannen fra ørkenen?`,en:`What did the man from the desert say?`},clues:[`essener`],yes:{nb:`Én dåp, i elva, for alle. Hva slags mann var Johannes?`,en:`One baptism, in the river, for everyone. What kind of man was John?`},no:{nb:`Det er ikke mannen fra ørkenen.`,en:`That is not the man from the desert.`}}],options:[{text:{nb:`Han krevde ærlighet der folk sto; ingen opprører, men en profet for alle`,en:`He asked honesty where people stood; no rebel, but a prophet for all`},feedback:{nb:`Riktig. Ikke for en lukket flokk, og ikke med sverd. Og tollere og soldater får spørre.`,en:`Right. Not for a closed flock, and not with the sword. And tax collectors and soldiers get to ask.`},correct:!0},{text:{nb:`Han ba alle forlate arbeidet og følge ham ut i ørkenen, slik mennene ved Dødehavet gjør`,en:`He told everyone to leave their work and follow him into the desert, as the men by the Dead Sea do`},feedback:{nb:`Nei. Tolleren fortsatte som toller, med rene hender, og soldaten forble soldat. Og mannen fra ørkenen sa selv at Johannes var annerledes.`,en:`No. The tax collector went on as a tax collector, with clean hands, and the soldier stayed a soldier. And the man from the desert said himself that John was different.`}},{text:{nb:`Han ba soldatene legge ned våpnene og gjøre opprør mot kongen som betalte dem`,en:`He told the soldiers to lay down their weapons and revolt against the king who paid them`},feedback:{nb:`Nei. Vær fornøyd med lønna, sa han, og press ingen for penger. Kongen fryktet ham likevel, for mengdens skyld.`,en:`No. Be content with your pay, he said, and extort money from no one. The king feared him all the same, because of the crowd.`}}],set:[`hva-gjore-lost`]},{id:`ved-elva`,question:{nb:`Hva skjedde ved Jordan, og i hvilken rekkefølge?`,en:`What happened at the Jordan, and in what order?`},clues:[`elva`,`kone`,`makerus`],steps:[{ask:{nb:`Finn vadestedet, den gamle kona og det soldaten sa om Makerus.`,en:`Find the ford, the old woman and what the soldier said about Machaerus.`},clues:[`elva`,`kone`,`makerus`],yes:{nb:`Elva, mengden og borgen. Sett det i rekkefølge.`,en:`The river, the crowds and the fortress. Put it in order.`},no:{nb:`Det hjelper ikke med rekkefølgen.`,en:`That does not help with the order.`}}],sequence:[{nb:`Guds ord kommer til Johannes i ørkenen, i Tiberius’ femtende år`,en:`The word of God comes to John in the wilderness, in Tiberius’ fifteenth year`},{nb:`Hele landet går ned til Jordan og lar seg døpe`,en:`The whole land goes down to the Jordan and is baptised`},{nb:`Folk spør hva de skal gjøre, og om han er Messias; han sier nei, en sterkere kommer`,en:`People ask what they are to do, and whether he is the Messiah; he says no, a stronger one is coming`},{nb:`Jesus kommer og lar seg døpe`,en:`Jesus comes and is baptised`},{nb:`Antipas fengsler Johannes i Makerus`,en:`Antipas imprisons John at Machaerus`}],explained:{nb:`Slik hang det sammen: en røst i ørkenen, et helt land i elva, og en fyrste som ikke tålte røsten.`,en:`So it fits together: a voice in the wilderness, a whole land in the river, and a ruler who could not bear the voice.`},set:[`ved-elva-lost`]}],objectives:[{text:{nb:`Snakk med Lukas`,en:`Talk to Luke`},doneBy:[`oppdrag`]},{text:{nb:`Snakk med disippelen, tolleren, soldaten, mannen fra ørkenen, skriveren og den gamle kona`,en:`Talk to the disciple, the tax collector, the soldier, the man from the desert, the scribe and the old woman`},doneBy:[`spor:disippel`,`spor:toller`,`spor:soldat`,`spor:essener`,`spor:skriver`,`spor:kone`]},{text:{nb:`Les sporene med eseldriveren, så finner du stien ned til elva`,en:`Read the tracks with the donkey driver, and you will find the path down to the river`},doneBy:[`sporene-lest`]},{text:{nb:`Gå ned til vadestedet og se deg om ved elva`,en:`Go down to the ford and look around by the river`},doneBy:[`spor:elva`,`spor:kamelhaar`,`spor:pilegrim`]},{text:{nb:`Les arkene og rullene i skriverommet`,en:`Read the sheets and scrolls in the writing room`},doneBy:[`spor:tidslinje`,`spor:jesaja`,`spor:malaki`,`spor:notat`]},{text:{nb:`Løs sakene i vitneboka`,en:`Solve the cases in the notebook`},doneBy:[`datering-lost`,`johannes-lost`,`daapen-lost`,`elia-lost`,`hva-gjore-lost`,`ved-elva-lost`]},{text:{nb:`Gå tilbake til Lukas`,en:`Go back to Luke`},doneBy:[`avsluttet`]}],rewards:[{flag:`datering-lost`,points:15,label:{nb:`Finn den andre Lysanias`,en:`Find the other Lysanias`}},{flag:`johannes-lost`,points:15,label:{nb:`Bli kjent med Johannes`,en:`Get to know John`}},{flag:`daapen-lost`,points:20,label:{nb:`Se det pinlige stå`,en:`See the awkward part stand`}},{flag:`elia-lost`,points:10,label:{nb:`Forstå Elia-spørsmålet`,en:`Understand the Elijah question`}},{flag:`hva-gjore-lost`,points:10,label:{nb:`Hør tollere og soldater`,en:`Hear tax collectors and soldiers`}},{flag:`ved-elva-lost`,points:10,label:{nb:`Sett elva i rekkefølge`,en:`Put the river in order`}},{flag:`avsluttet`,points:10,label:{nb:`Fullfør dagen med Lukas`,en:`Finish the day with Luke`}},{flag:`vannet-maalt`,points:10,label:{nb:`Mål opp vannet`,en:`Measure the water`},side:!0},{flag:`spor:driver`,points:5,label:{nb:`Hør om veien til Makerus`,en:`Hear about the road to Machaerus`},side:!0},{flag:`spor:pilegrim`,points:5,label:{nb:`Møt pilegrimen ved elva`,en:`Meet the pilgrim at the river`},side:!0},{flag:`vadet`,points:10,label:{nb:`Gå over Jordan stein for stein`,en:`Cross the Jordan stone by stone`},side:!0},{flag:`maaltid-levert`,points:10,label:{nb:`Finn honning og gresshopper til pilegrimen`,en:`Find honey and locusts for the pilgrim`},side:!0},{flag:`sporene-lest`,points:10,label:{nb:`Les sporene`,en:`Read the tracks`},side:!0}],inventory:[{icon:`🍯`,label:{nb:`Honning og gresshopper`,en:`Honey and locusts`},flags:[`honning`,`gresshopper`],goneWhen:`maaltid-levert`}],ambience:[{sound:`garden`,x:14,y:5,radius:7},{sound:`market`,x:11,y:13,radius:5}],goal:[`avsluttet`],solution:`lukas.disippel.toller.soldat.essener.skriver.kone.jente.driver.dor-vadestedet.stein-1.stein-2.stein-3.stein-4.elva.kamelhaar.pilegrim.bikube.sivet.pilegrim.dor-ut-vadestedet.dor-skriverommet.tidslinje.jesaja.malaki.notat.dor-ut-skriverommet.datering.johannes.daapen.elia.hva-gjore.ved-elva.lukas`.split(`.`)};export{e as default};